  "name": "dead-code-fixer",
  "description": "Finds and removes dead code across a repository too large for one context window. Static analyzers and a repository-wide reference count propose candidates, Haiku subagents verify each one through three independent lenses, and confirmed-dead code is deleted in waves gated by the project's type-check and tests, with one commit per wave, round after round until nothing new dies. Use when the user asks to find, remove, prune or clean up dead code, unused code, unused exports, unreachable functions, orphaned files, or unused dependencies.",
